# <%= name %>

A Roblox game built with [KRF](https://kevmp.github.io/KRF/) `<%= runtime.package %>@<%= runtime.version %>`.

## Setup

```bash
npm install
npm run dev
```

`npm run dev` opens `<%= name %>.rbxl` in Roblox Studio and serves the project with Rojo. Connect the Rojo plugin, then press Play. Commit `wally.lock`.
<% if (options.mode === "hybrid") { -%>

This is a Hybrid project: Rojo syncs `src` and `Packages`, and `<%= name %>.rbxl` owns the world. Save your world in it; `npm run dev` creates it once and never rebuilds it.
<% } -%>

## Scripts

| Script | Does |
| --- | --- |
| `npm run dev` | Builds and opens the place in Studio and serves it with Rojo; `-- --no-open` only serves |
<% if (options.mode === "hybrid") { -%>
| `npm run build` | Builds `build/<%= name %>.rbxl` from the starter world, without touching your place |
<% } else { -%>
| `npm run build` | Builds `<%= name %>.rbxl` |
<% } -%>
| `npm test` | Runs the Jest specs in `tests` inside Roblox Studio |
| `npm run test:studio` | Plays the game in Studio with a server and two clients and checks that KRF starts |
| `npm run format` | Formats `src` and `tests` |
| `npm run check` | Checks formatting, lints and type checks without changing files |
| `npm run createAction`, `createTag`, `createResource`, `createProperty`, `createController`, `createCommand`, `createHint`, `createDomain` | Creates a definition; see [Definition Generators](https://kevmp.github.io/KRF/definition-generators) |
